; sayBasics.inix -- a live test of DbDo, played by tidy after a build.
;
; Tidy plays every macro in scripts\tests when DbDo is closed, a screen reader is running, and the macro, the program
; or the key file changed since its last pass. It opens the build just made, presses these keys, listens to the reader
; and checks what Windows shows. It only says things and opens and closes the Alternate Menu, so it changes nothing.
; Play it by hand with: scripts\runMacro scripts\tests\sayBasics.inix

FileTask = macroScript
App = DbDo
Name = The Say family speaks, and the Key Describer describes

[steps]
; START AT THE GRID (27 November 2026): the run of 12:41 began with focus in a list DbDo had left open, so the
; first two keys spoke nothing and the second reached another window. Escape twice closes any such list first.
Press Escape twice
Say Filter and Order
Expect speech filter
Say Position
Expect speech percent
Alternate Menu
Expect window Alternate Menu
Press Escape
Key Describer Toggle
Say Filter and Order
Expect speech filter and order
Key Describer Toggle
